    "utterance": "I'm updating our safeguarding card for a resident-money discrepancy. Who receives the first escalation now, what part does Finance keep, and which current role name and outside-agency sharing route should the card use?",
    "status": "completed",
    "displayed_text": "Escalate the concern first to the Alderbridge Safeguarding Lead \u2014 the policy replaces the previous Finance Manager first\u2011route so a financial concern is reported directly to the Safeguarding Lead as the initial escalation contact.\n\nFinance retains and supports the financial-record aspect: sites must record every personal-allowance transaction at the time it occurs (with countersignature above the site low-value threshold), reconcile each resident's personal-allowance balance weekly and investigate discrepancies the same day, and the Finance Manager supports the subsequent financial record review and audits resident fund records quarterly.\n\nUse the organisation-level job title \u2018Safeguarding Lead\u2019 on the card for the internal contact, and show the authorised outside-agency referral route as the local authority safeguarding team (refer within one working day for concerns meeting the local threshold); additional specific external routes identified in the safeguarding suite include referring to the Office of the Public Guardian where an attorney/deputy may be acting outside authority and to Action Fraud where suspected fraud or a scam is involved.",
